\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Architectural comparison of hallucination verification paradigms. (A) Traditional monolithic black-box verification passes entire paragraphs to neural judges, leading to attention dilution and token overlap failure. (B) HalDetect's proposed type-directed neuro-symbolic triage decomposes prose into atomic 5-tuples and dispatches them to specialized deterministic ALUs.}}{2}{figure.caption.8}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end HalDetect verification pipeline. Unconstrained generative text is atomized into typed 5-tuples $\langle S, P, O, T, M \rangle $ with forward antecedent anaphora resolution, routed via a sub-$0.05\text {ms}$ deterministic classifier, verified across domain-specific symbolic ALUs and calibrated NLI, and evaluated via a 3-valued conjunction DAG.}}{11}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Multi-Aspect Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) Conjunction Engine. Compound propositions containing multiple factual dimensions are decomposed into parallel verification micro-checks and resolved via 3-valued conjunction logic.}}{16}{figure.caption.13}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Chronological evolution and lineage of benchmark datasets across five developmental phases, culminating in the symmetrical 1,000-claim Master Corpus and the 1,798-proposition Track 2 Multi-LLM generative testbed.}}{18}{figure.caption.15}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces The Attention Dilution Breakdown. When an LLM asserts an incorrect transistor count for the Apple M3 Max, continuous neural cross-encoders perceive 85\% matching contextual tokens and emit Entailment. HalDetect's Dimensional SI ALU isolates numerical values and triggers a decisive Contradiction verdict.}}{26}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Coverage vs. Selective Accuracy Pareto frontier. By varying the rejection threshold $\tau _{\text {abstain}}$, HalDetect traverses from 97.60\% accuracy at 100\% coverage to 98.18\% selective accuracy at high confidence ($N = 494$).}}{29}{figure.caption.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Expected Calibration Error (ECE) 10-bin reliability diagram. Predicted model confidence aligns closely with observed empirical accuracy across all 10 confidence deciles ($ECE = 0.0888$, Brier score = $0.0297$).}}{30}{figure.caption.25}%
